WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.810
- [Instructor] We are told

00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:04.150
fill in the table with whole numbers

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:09.150
to make 10.74 in two different ways.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:11.860
So pause this video and see
if you can figure that out.

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:12.930
So you really need to fill out

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:14.900
what would you put in here

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:17.923
for this to be a representation of 10.74?

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:20.020
All right, now let's do it together

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:22.690
and I'm gonna rewrite the
number a little bit larger

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:27.150
so we can really inspect the place values.

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:30.150
So one way to think about
it is we have zero ones

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:32.390
and then we have one 10.

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:33.890
But they don't express it that way.

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:36.080
They don't say one 10
and zero ones up here.

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:38.750
They just say 10 ones,
but that's reasonable.

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:40.860
So when they're saying 10 ones here,

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:43.920
they are referring to those 10 ones,

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:45.870
or you could view that
as one 10 and zero ones.

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:47.450
Either way, you have 10 ones,

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:49.700
and then if you move
one decimal place over,

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:52.160
this 7/10, well that makes sense.

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:54.070
You have a seven in the tenths place

00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:57.640
and then this 4/100 makes sense.

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:01.350
You have four in the hundredths place.

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:02.900
But now let's see what
they're doing over here.

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:06.560
So once again, they're
saying no 10s, but 10 ones.

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:09.010
So that is actually the same.

00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:12.760
We could say one 10 and zero
ones, or we could say 10 ones.

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:13.890
And now over here,

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:16.720
they've reduced the number of tenths.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:17.960
You know, you're like,
hey, what's going on?

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:21.130
I have, there looks
like there's 7/10 here.

00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:23.940
But one way to think about
it is they're regrouping

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:25.970
from one place to another.

00:01:25.970 --> 00:01:27.710
And so what they've done is

00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:30.030
they've taken that extra 10th

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:31.890
and they've put it someplace.

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:33.380
And the only other place they could put it

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:35.830
is in the hundredths place.

00:01:35.830 --> 00:01:40.830
So if I were to take a
tenth from the tenths place,

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:44.070
a tenth is worth 10 hundredths.

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:46.130
So one way to think about it is,

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:49.130
you're taking a tenth from there,

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:51.040
so now this is going to be,

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:53.603
this is going to be 6/10,

00:01:54.470 --> 00:01:57.750
and if you, where you're
going to put that tenth,

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.910
well you could put it
in the hundredths place,

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:01.973
but a tenth is going to be 10/100.

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:06.920
So if you add 10/100 to the
4/100 that are already there,

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:11.200
well, that is going to give you 14/100,

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:14.350
so we would put a 14 right over there.

00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:16.120
Let's do another example

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:17.900
just to really make
sure we're understanding

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:19.250
what's going on.

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:22.220
So once again, they say fill
in the table with whole numbers

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:25.930
to make 5.4 in three different ways.

00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:29.330
So pause this video and see
if you can have a go at it.

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:30.260
All right.

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:31.970
So I'm gonna write the number,

00:02:31.970 --> 00:02:33.653
so we have 5.4,

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:38.550
and in this first row, this
is maybe the most standard way

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:41.270
or traditional way of interpreting 5.4.

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:43.160
In our ones place, you have a five

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:44.550
and you see that, five ones,

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:46.460
and in our tenths place,

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:48.550
we have a four,

00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:50.810
and that's what they have
right over here, 4/10.

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:53.470
But what are they doing
in this second row?

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:56.551
Well, they're saying 24/10.

00:02:56.551 --> 00:03:00.920
24/10, so somehow, in
way to think about it,

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:02.690
in the tenths place,

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:06.140
they were able to add 20/10.

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:11.140
So they went from 4/10 to 24/10.

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:14.490
So if you're adding 20/10 here,

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:18.187
they must have taken it
away from some other place.

00:03:18.187 --> 00:03:22.870
20/10 is the same thing as two ones,

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:25.700
so they must have taken
two ones away from here.

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:27.720
So they took two ones away from here,

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:32.250
so this would be three ones and now 24/10.

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:34.760
So we could put a three right over there.

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:36.183
And you can verify that.

00:03:36.183 --> 00:03:39.940
24/10 is the same thing as two wholes

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:43.823
and, or two ones and 4/10 or 2.4.

00:03:44.992 --> 00:03:49.473
2.4 plus three is going
to be equal to 5.4.

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:52.460
All right.

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:55.670
So here, we only have one one,

00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:58.770
and so what happened
to the other four ones?

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:02.270
Well, they must have been
transferred to the tenths place.

00:04:02.270 --> 00:04:04.320
So let me rewrite the number.

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:08.190
So if we were to take four
ones away from the ones place,

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:09.910
so we're taking four away from this,

00:04:09.910 --> 00:04:11.580
we only have one left,

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:14.030
and what would happen if I
transferred those four ones

00:04:14.030 --> 00:04:15.630
to the tenths place?

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:18.440
Well, then there would be 40/10.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:21.160
Four ones are 40/10,

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:25.860
so we would add 40 to 40/10 over here,

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:27.490
so we already have 4/10,

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:30.920
so this would become 44/10.

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:32.580
44/10.

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:33.503
And we're done.

